Subject: [PATCH 2/3] pci: pci_find_capability() falls back to dev->pcie_cap

Companion to the orphan PCIe Express cap adoption patch in probe.c.

set_pcie_port_type() now records the orphan cap location in
dev->pcie_cap when the legacy cap chain doesn't link to it. But many
callers (including _pci_add_cap_save_buffer(), aer_init, and others)
re-derive the cap location by calling pci_find_capability(dev,
PCI_CAP_ID_EXP) directly, and those calls still return 0 because they
just walk the legacy chain.

Without this fallback, pci_save_state() later fails with:
   "buffer not found in pci_save_pcie_state"
and AER/Rebar buffers are never allocated.

Make pci_find_capability(dev, PCI_CAP_ID_EXP) return dev->pcie_cap when
the legacy chain walk fails. Safe: dev->pcie_cap is only set when our
orphan scan already validated the cap header.

Apply to: drivers/pci/pci.c

--- a/drivers/pci/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci.c
@@ -480,6 +480,18 @@ u8 pci_find_capability(struct pci_dev *dev, int cap)
 	if (pos)
 		pos = __pci_find_next_cap(dev->bus, dev->devfn, pos, cap);

+	/*
+	 * v2 fix for the orphaned-PCIe-cap quirk (AMD RDNA4 / Navi48):
+	 * if the legacy cap chain didn't find PCI_CAP_ID_EXP but our
+	 * earlier orphan scan in set_pcie_port_type() did and recorded
+	 * it in dev->pcie_cap, use that. Without this, callers like
+	 * _pci_add_cap_save_buffer() never allocate the PCIe save buffer
+	 * and pci_save_state() later fails with "buffer not found in
+	 * pci_save_pcie_state".
+	 */
+	if (!pos && cap == PCI_CAP_ID_EXP && dev->pcie_cap)
+		pos = dev->pcie_cap;
+
 	return pos;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(pci_find_capability);

NOTE: For other kernel versions, locate the body of pci_find_capability
in drivers/pci/pci.c (a short function ~10 lines that calls
__pci_bus_find_cap_start and __pci_find_next_cap), and insert the
fallback block before the final `return pos;`.
